From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chinohana <chinohana@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 21:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] selinux: allow ksu to read domain-typed proc entries

Android labels per-process procfs inodes with the process domain rather
than a regular file_type.  The explicit Linux 4.19 rule table therefore
does not cover /proc/<pid>, even though it grants ksu read access to
file_type objects.  A manager root shell consequently dies while looking
up its own file descriptors after the credential transition succeeds.

Grant read-only access from ksu to procfs objects carrying a domain type.
Keep the legacy test kernel enforcing and do not restore the upstream
permissive or wildcard rules.
---
 kernel/selinux/rules.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/selinux/rules.c b/kernel/selinux/rules.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/kernel/selinux/rules.c
+++ b/kernel/selinux/rules.c
@@ -92,6 +92,16 @@ static bool ksu_apply_legacy_kernelsu_rules(struct policydb *db)
         { "init", KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "process", "sigchld" },
         { "init", KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "process", "noatsecure" },
         { "init", KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "process", "rlimitinh" },
+        /* Android procfs PID inodes inherit their process domain type. */
+        { KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "domain", "dir", "search" },
+        { KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "domain", "dir", "open" },
+        { KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "domain", "dir", "read" },
+        { KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "domain", "dir", "getattr" },
+        { KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "domain", "file", "open" },
+        { KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "domain", "file", "read" },
+        { KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "domain", "file", "getattr" },
+        { KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "domain", "lnk_file", "read" },
+        { KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "domain", "lnk_file", "getattr" },
         { KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "domain", "process", "getattr" },
         { KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "domain", "process", "getpgid" },
         { KERNEL_SU_DOMAIN, "domain", "process", "signal" },
-- 
